border-*-style: the none, hidden, solid and dashed longhands, the border-style shorthand, and the style in each border-<side>
shorthand (width, style, color). A side without a drawn style has no width; a drawn one without a declared width is medium (3px).
Dashed sides follow Chromium (box_border_painter.cc, styled_stroke_data.cc): the dash and gap per width, the dash count fitted
to the path, a square side dashed over its whole outer edge and mitred at the corners, a rounded border dashed along its
centerline from the top edge after the top-left radius. A rounded side whose corners have no inner radius is dashed along the
centerline too (Chromium strokes it straight).
CSS Backgrounds 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-backgrounds-3/#border-style

